      "id": "bdd10f41-1124-41c0-b9c2-b9811c4ab2e8",
      "notes": "Grounds the LLM in the actual regulation text instead of letting it invent citations. Points at a local Chroma REST endpoint - swap for your own vector store URL."
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "method": "POST",
        "url": "https://api.groq.com/openai/v1/chat/completions",
        "authentication": "genericCredentialType",
        "genericAuthType": "httpHeaderAuth",
        "sendHeaders": true,
        "headerParameters": {
          "parameters": [
            {
              "name": "Content-Type",
              "value": "application/json"
            }
          ]
        },
        "sendBody": true,
        "specifyBody": "json",
        "jsonBody": "={{ {\n  \"model\": \"llama-3.3-70b-versatile\",\n  \"temperature\": 0.1,\n  \"messages\": [\n    {\n      \"role\": \"system\",\n      \"content\": \"You are a bank General Counsel drafting a transaction reconstruction cover note for a law enforcement request. Only state facts present in the supplied data and the supplied regulatory clause. Do not invent figures, dates, or citations. If a required field is missing, say so explicitly instead of guessing.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"role\": \"user\",\n      \"content\": (\n        \"Compile a short reconstruction bundle cover note for account \" + $(\"Retention Gateway\").item.json.body.account_number +\n        \", covering \" + $(\"Retention Gateway\").item.json.body.start_date + \" to \" + $(\"Retention Gateway\").item.json.body.end_date +\n        \".\\n\\nRegulatory clause to cite (from RAG retrieval):\\n\" + $json.clause +\n        \"\\n\\nTransaction records to certify:\\n\" + JSON.stringify($(\"Search Transactions\").all().map(i => i.json)) +\n        \"\\n\\nConfirm which of the four mandated fields (date, currency+amount, nature/type, account identifier) are present for each record, and note any that are missing.\"\n      )\n    }\n  ]\n} }}",
        "options": {}
      },
      "name": "AI Compile Cover Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "typeVersion": 4.2,
      "position": [
        1056,
        448
      ],
      "id": "03062a2f-254b-451d-9b03-dc7def4a865e",
      "credentials": {
        "httpHeaderAuth": {
          "id": "7en4gTUrMPAy27zp",
          "name": "Header Auth account"
        }
      },
      "notes": "Calls Groq's OpenAI-compatible chat completions endpoint directly via HTTP Request (n8n has no native Groq node). Create an 'Header Auth' credential named e.g. 'Groq API Key' with header 'Authorization: Bearer <your_groq_api_key>' and attach it here. Single, narrow, low-temperature call - drafting text only, grounded in the RAG clause + real DB rows. It never decides whether to freeze/deliver/hold; that stays in Postgres/IF logic."
    },
